  "description": "The AT28C64B is a 64 Kbit (8,192 x 8) byte-wide parallel EEPROM with a JEDEC-standard 28-pin pinout, accessed like a static RAM via 13 address lines and 8 data I/O lines under /CE, /OE, and /WE control. It runs from a single 5V supply with 150 ns access time, supports automatic page write of up to 64 bytes, and includes hardware and software data protection. Endurance is 100,000 cycles with 10-year retention. Its standout trait is being a hobbyist favorite for retro CPU/ROM projects and homebrew computers needing an in-system reprogrammable parallel ROM.",
