  "gotchas": [
    "JEDEC 28-pin pinout matches 2764/27C64 EPROM and 6264 SRAM closely but not identically; pin 1 and pins 26/27 differ, verify before socket-swapping",
    "pins 1 and 26 are NC on the DIP; do not assume they are address lines like on larger 28-pin parts",
    "default 10 ms page write timer means a naive byte-at-a-time loop is very slow; use page write or poll I/O7 (DATA polling / toggle bit)",
    "software data protection can be enabled and will silently block writes until the unlock sequence is issued; a 'dead' chip is often just SDP-locked",
    "/WE-controlled and /CE-controlled write timings differ; hold the other signal stable during the active write strobe",
    "this is 5V only; do not drive address/data from 3.3V logic expecting reliable VIH without checking levels"
  ],
